@startuml
!theme plain
title D06 route send status (SendStatus)

[*] --> CURRENT : POST /routes/{id}/send\nall checks and the LEZ guard pass
CURRENT --> SUPERSEDED : a newer send of the same route\n(same transaction as its insert)
SUPERSEDED --> [*]

note right of CURRENT
  At most one CURRENT send per route: the insert runs under
  a row lock on the route and re-counts CURRENT rows; a loser
  answers 409 and its transaction rolls back.
  The driver sees CURRENT sends first, then SUPERSEDED ones.
end note

note bottom
  Sends are never updated otherwise and never deleted by the
  application: they are the delivery history (BR-054).
  A refused send (400/422/502) creates no row.
end note
@enduml
